# Copy to .env and fill in. Never commit .env itself.
#
# The first two are the same values as src/integrations/supabase/client.ts. The
# publishable key is designed to be public; it only proves who is signed in.
NITRO_SUPABASE_URL=https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
NITRO_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=sb_publishable_<publishable-key>

# SECRET. Server-only, never committed, never shared.
#
# Needed by the admin panel, to create accounts and switch people's access, and by
# the voucher numbering endpoint, which has to read voucher numbers that the
# signed-in preparer is not allowed to see. Nothing under src/ reads it. On
# Vercel set it under
#   Settings > Environment Variables with Production scope, then redeploy:
#   Vercel > Settings > Environment Variables > Add Environment Variable
#     Name:  NITRO_SUPABASE_SERVICE_KEY
#     Scope: Production
#
# Find it in Supabase under Project Settings > API Keys > Secret key. It begins
# sb_secret_. The publishable key will NOT work: it bypasses row level security
# only for the service role, and those two routes need that.
#
# Without it everything else still works: sign-in, vouchers, per-preparer
# workspaces, monthly approval. Only "Add person", access toggles, password
# resets and collision-free voucher numbering stop.
NITRO_SUPABASE_SERVICE_KEY=sb_secret_<secret-key>